<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Dec oil exports up 20.2 pct on year - TDB.</title>
<headline>Singapore Dec oil exports up 20.2 pct on year - TDB.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's domestic oil exports rose a nominal 20.2 percent year-on-year in December to Singapore $1.399 billion, the Trade Development Board (TDB) said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Domestic exports of oil rose by 20.2 percent in the month. This was due mainly to the continued surge of 19.4 percent in oil prices due to the cold weather in Europe and U.S. and a shortage of heating oil stocks,&quot; the TDB said.</p>
<p>The rise in exports was expected as prices of most petroleum products such as diesel and kerosene hit new post-Gulf War records due to peak winter demand.  </p>
<p>However, oil exports were 4.6 percent lower in value terms in December than November's S$1.466 billion.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
